    "long_instructions": "## Read a Finished Project\r\nThis is the finished project your students are aiming for. Read it the way they will, by tracing each row of the data table into a line of code.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Directions\r\n \r\nLook through a finished classifier.\r\n \r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Open the finished [Project Planning Guide](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ela5mpW_qkhmoFLJD9C9CIRCNg7Ux8l97Mf1fjnViyI/edit?usp=sharing) and find the Step 3 table.\r\n- In the code, find the dictionaries for the Train rows.\r\n- Run the code. `test_image` matches image 12 in the guide. Does the prediction match its category?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n::: details [**See a solution**]\r\n\r\nThe code runs as written. The output is:\r\n```\r\nPredicted category for test image: River\r\n```\r\n\r\n`test_image` matches image 12 in the guide, a River, and one River training image has exactly the same features (distance 0), so the prediction is correct.\r\n:::\r\n",
